%[text] %[text:anchor:T_674BCFA4] # Introduction to Engineering: 
%[text] %[text:anchor:T_FDB00D6B] # A Hands-On Exploration with Arduino
%[text] 
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_2CF9C085] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_035F075E] ### [**SupportArduino.m**](file:Scripts/SupportArduino.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[0,469],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:48f0) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Check their Arduino board compatibility.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Install MATLAB and Simulink support packages for Arduino Hardware.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Setup ThingSpeak channel for IoT.</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E8C62B23] ### [BlinkToSOS.m](file:Scripts/BlinkToSOS.m)
%[text:table]{"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:31af) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Learn the fundamental type of signals supported on and Arduino board.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Wire a simple LED to their Arduino board.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Control the LED from a simple blink to encoding Morse code</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_23B77A06] ### [**ReactionAnalyzer.m**](file:Scripts/ReactionAnalyzer.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[0,469],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:4461) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Learn how to control Arduino with a Stateflow diagram.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Learn data analysis techniques.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Write and export experiment report from MATLAB.</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51CBB9CC] ### [**GreenhouseControl.m**](file:Scripts/GreenhouseControl.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,469],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:1559) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Use a temperature sensor.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Develop a control algorithm.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Test their control algorithm.</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B7E2AA17] ### [**GreenhouseModel.m**](file:Scripts/GreenhouseModel.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,469],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:88ef) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Use a Simscape thermal model.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Simulate the greenhouse over a full year of data.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Test multiple fans to validate the design.</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_A398ED41] ### [**ConnectedGreenhouse.m**](file:Scripts/ConnectedGreenhouse.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,469],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:2041) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Learn how to read and write from a ThingSpeak channel.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Log the temperature in the greenhouse on their own channel.</p><p>$\\bullet${"editStyle":"visual"} Create an alert when the temperature exceeds the acceptable range.</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
